ments (lines 64–68), Deliverables (lines 164–167), Success Criteria (lines 192–198); Success Criteria line 193 cites `25 mutations` instead of `23 mutations` | diverged |\n\n## Must-fix\n- `Requirements` FR-2 drops `CONFLICT` from the `COLLECT:` contract line (`COLLECT: OK|MISSING` instead of `COLLECT: OK|MISSING|CONFLICT`) — Under `## Requirements`, the `FR-2` bullet specifies the CLI stdout token contract as `COLLECT: OK|MISSING path=\u003cdocs path\u003e delivered=report-file|out|none [forced=1]`, omitting the `CONFLICT` verdict required by `docs/01-plan/features/audit-report-docs-copy.spec.md` (FR-2, AC-2.5, AC-2.6a, AC-5.4) and referenced elsewhere in `docs/01-plan/features/audit-report-docs-copy.plan.md` (Goals line 37 and Architecture Considerations lines 118–125). Because FR-2 defines the CLI output contract and helper-registry token set, an implementer or test author following Requirements FR-2 literally would omit `CONFLICT` from the token grammar.\n  class: build\n  quote: docs/01-plan/features/audit-report-docs-copy.plan.md › `COLLECT: OK|MISSING path=\u003cdocs path\u003e`\n  quote: docs/01-plan/features/audit-report-docs-copy.spec.md › `COLLECT: OK|MISSING|CONFLICT path=\u003cdocs path\u003e`\n- `Success Criteria` cites `25 mutations` in `collect_report.json`, contradicting `23 mutations` in Requirements, Deliverables, Version History, and Spec AC-6.3 — In `docs/01-plan/features/audit-report-docs-copy.plan.md`, `## Success Criteria` line 193 requires `MUTATION: ALL_CAUGHT` on `collect_report.json` with `(25 mutations, every connection dropped AND forced, fall-through paths included)`, whereas `## Requirements` FR-6 (line 65), `## Deliverables` (line 166), `## Version History` (lines 220 and 222), and `docs/01-plan/features/audit-report-docs-copy.spec.md` AC-6.3 (line 242) all specify `23` mutations.\n  class: measurement\n  quote: docs/01-plan/features/audit-report-docs-copy.plan.md › `(25 mutations, every connection dropped`\n  quote: docs/01-plan/fea